      "writtenOn": "2023-09-11T05:15:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Eric,\nFrom the fuzzer, there is no need to explicitly call `native_handle_delete()` on `rawHandle` as it will be called from `hidl_handle::freeHandle()` of system/libhidl/base/HidlSupport.cpp [Reference: https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:system/libhidl/base/HidlSupport.cpp;l\u003d132;drc\u003d0a5abc5903d20b76024f6ffeb9e27ce335f2cf69;bpv\u003d0;bpt\u003d1]\n\nFor more details about the entire call flow, you could refer to https://b.corp.google.com/issues/232476708#comment2",
      "parentUuid": "78470776_3b0164ad",
      "revId": "e8f0cf29494e14875ccdaa9ff87d350fb223e7f4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e48cbaeb_449469c1",
        "filename": "automotive/vehicle/2.0/default/tests/fuzzer/VehicleManager_fuzzer.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 167,
      "author": {
        "id": 1594173
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-11T17:01:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`native_handle_clone` creates a new copy of the handle.\n\nsystem/core/libcutils/native_handle.cpp\n```\n    native_handle_t* clone \u003d native_handle_create(handle-\u003enumFds, handle-\u003enumInts);\n    ...\n    memcpy(\u0026clone-\u003edata[handle-\u003enumFds], \u0026handle-\u003edata[handle-\u003enumFds],\n           sizeof(int) * handle-\u003enumInts);\n```\n\nhidl_handle only deletes the cloned copy. The original copy is still owned by the caller. It needs to deleted explicitly before returning from this method.",
      "parentUuid": "13e3a847_60dd826e",
      "revId": "e8f0cf29494e14875ccdaa9ff87d350fb223e7f4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
